<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · city</p><h1 class="enc-title">Sulaymaniyah</h1><p class="enc-meta">Also known as Slemani, Sulaimani</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Sulaymaniyah is a city in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kurdistan">Kurdistan</a> Region of north-eastern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/iraq">Iraq</a>, near the Iranian border. It was founded in 1784 by <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ibrahim-pasha-baban">Ibrahim Pasha Baban</a> as the capital of the Baban <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/emirate">emirate</a> and named after the Ottoman governor of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/baghdad">Baghdad</a>, Sulayman Pasha. It became a centre of Kurdish culture and nationalism, and in the 1920s Shaikh <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mahmud-barzanji">Mahmud Barzanji</a> proclaimed a Kingdom of Kurdistan there.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/sulaymaniyah.jpg" alt="Sulaymaniyah" width="320" height="213" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Diyar Muhammed · CC BY-SA 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Sulaymaniyah_City_-_Grand_Millenium_Hotel.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
